:R-HSA-196807  a            owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0019674 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Nicotinate (niacin) and nicotinamide are precursors of the coenzymes nicotinamide-adenine dinucleotide (NAD+) and nicotinamide-adenine dinucleotide phosphate (NADP+). When NAD+ and NADP+ are interchanged in a reaction with their reduced forms, NADH and NADPH respectively, they are important cofactors in several hundred redox reactions. Nicotinate is synthesized from 2-amino-3-carboxymuconate semialdehyde, an intermediate in the catabolism of the essential amino acid tryptophan (Magni et al. 2004)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Nicotinate metabolism" ;
        layout:x            "3225" ;
        layout:y            "75" ;
        dc:contributor      "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7476-6306" , "Authored: Jassal, B, 2007-04-24 08:38:46" , "Edited: Jassal, Bijay, 2016-09-23" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
